WEBVTT

00:00.620 --> 00:02.780
Now let's do a really
interesting problem.

00:02.780 --> 00:05.290
So I have y equals x,
and y is equal to x

00:05.290 --> 00:07.840
squared minus 2x
right over here.

00:07.840 --> 00:09.530
And we're going to
rotate the region

00:09.530 --> 00:11.020
in between these two functions.

00:11.020 --> 00:13.277
So that's this region
right over here.

00:13.277 --> 00:15.610
And we're not going to rotate
it just around the x-axis,

00:15.610 --> 00:19.360
we're going to rotate it around
the horizontal line y equals 4.

00:19.360 --> 00:21.454
So we're going to
rotate it around this.

00:21.454 --> 00:23.870
And if we do that, we'll get
a shape that looks like this.

00:23.870 --> 00:26.550
I drew it ahead of time, just
so I could draw it nicely.

00:26.550 --> 00:30.210
And as you can see, it looks
like some type of a vase

00:30.210 --> 00:32.060
with a hole at the bottom.

00:32.060 --> 00:34.520
And so what we're going to do
is attempt to do this using,

00:34.520 --> 00:36.395
I guess you'd call it
the washer method which

00:36.395 --> 00:37.800
is a variant of the disk method.

00:37.800 --> 00:39.790
So let's construct a washer.

00:39.790 --> 00:42.350
So let's look at a given x.

00:42.350 --> 00:45.520
So let's say an x
right over here.

00:45.520 --> 00:47.750
So let's say that we're
at an x right over there.

00:47.750 --> 00:48.370
And what we're
going to do is we're

00:48.370 --> 00:50.160
going to rotate this region.

00:50.160 --> 00:54.090
We're going to give
it some depth, dx.

00:54.090 --> 00:55.010
So that is dx.

00:55.010 --> 00:57.120
We're going to rotate
this around the line y

00:57.120 --> 00:57.840
is equal to 4.

00:57.840 --> 01:02.580
So if you were to visualize it
over here, you have some depth.

01:02.580 --> 01:05.472
And when you rotate it
around, the inner radius

01:05.472 --> 01:07.680
is going to look like the
inner radius of our washer.

01:07.680 --> 01:09.440
It's going to look
something like that.

01:12.210 --> 01:13.900
And then the outer
radius of our washer

01:13.900 --> 01:17.420
is going to contour
around x squared minus 2x.

01:17.420 --> 01:21.780
So it's going to
look something--

01:21.780 --> 01:23.703
my best attempt
to draw it-- it's

01:23.703 --> 01:25.440
going to look
something like that.

01:27.950 --> 01:30.810
And of course, our washer
is going to have some depth.

01:30.810 --> 01:32.250
So let me draw the depth.

01:32.250 --> 01:35.950
So it's going to
have some depth, dx.

01:35.950 --> 01:39.940
So this is my best attempt at
drawing some of that the depth.

01:39.940 --> 01:42.970
So this is the
depth of our washer.

01:42.970 --> 01:45.440
And then just to make the face
of the washer a little bit

01:45.440 --> 01:47.230
clearer, let me do it
in this green color.

01:47.230 --> 01:49.440
So the face of the
washer is going

01:49.440 --> 01:52.310
to be all of this business.

01:52.310 --> 01:57.060
All of this business is going
to be the face of our washer.

01:57.060 --> 01:59.350
So if we can figure
out the volume of one

01:59.350 --> 02:01.210
of these washers for a
given x, then we just

02:01.210 --> 02:03.240
have to sum up all of
the washers for all

02:03.240 --> 02:05.919
of the x's in our interval.

02:05.919 --> 02:07.710
So let's see if we can
set up the integral,

02:07.710 --> 02:09.990
and maybe in the
next video we'll

02:09.990 --> 02:13.820
just forge ahead and actually
evaluate the integral.

02:13.820 --> 02:15.964
So let's think about the
volume of the washer.

02:15.964 --> 02:17.630
To think about the
volume of the washer,

02:17.630 --> 02:19.580
we really just have to
think about the area

02:19.580 --> 02:21.510
of the face of the washer.

02:21.510 --> 02:26.510
So area of "face"--
put face in quotes--

02:26.510 --> 02:28.380
is going to be equal to what?

02:28.380 --> 02:30.670
Well, it would be the
area of the washer--

02:30.670 --> 02:32.880
if it wasn't a washer,
if it was just a coin--

02:32.880 --> 02:35.441
and then subtract out
the area of the part

02:35.441 --> 02:36.440
that you're cutting out.

02:36.440 --> 02:38.890
So the area of the
washer if it didn't

02:38.890 --> 02:40.750
have a hole in the
middle would just

02:40.750 --> 02:44.285
be pi times the
outer radius squared.

02:48.150 --> 02:51.090
It would be pi times
this radius squared,

02:51.090 --> 02:52.950
that we could call
the outer radius.

02:52.950 --> 02:55.320
And since it's a washer,
we need to subtract out

02:55.320 --> 02:57.030
the area of this inner circle.

02:57.030 --> 03:05.500
So minus pi times
inner radius squared.

03:05.500 --> 03:07.000
So we really just
have to figure out

03:07.000 --> 03:11.160
what the outer and inner radius,
or radii I should say, are.

03:11.160 --> 03:12.710
So let's think about it.

03:12.710 --> 03:19.971
So our outer radius is
going to be equal to what?

03:19.971 --> 03:21.470
Well, we can visualize
it over here.

03:21.470 --> 03:23.610
This is our outer
radius, which is also

03:23.610 --> 03:27.770
going to be equal to
that right over there.

03:27.770 --> 03:29.720
So that's the distance
between y equals

03:29.720 --> 03:32.440
4 and the function that's
defining our outside.

03:38.250 --> 03:40.520
So this is essentially,
this height right over here,

03:40.520 --> 03:45.280
is going to be equal to 4
minus x squared minus 2x.

03:45.280 --> 03:48.000
I'm just finding the distance
or the height between these two

03:48.000 --> 03:48.900
functions.

03:48.900 --> 03:52.140
So the outer radius is
going to be 4 minus this,

03:52.140 --> 03:55.100
minus x squared minus
2x, which is just 4

03:55.100 --> 03:58.520
minus x squared plus 2x.

03:58.520 --> 03:59.850
Now, what is the inner radius?

04:05.080 --> 04:06.830
What is that going to be?

04:06.830 --> 04:11.550
Well, that's just going to
be this distance between y

04:11.550 --> 04:13.480
equals 4 and y equals x.

04:13.480 --> 04:15.265
So it's just going
to be 4 minus x.

04:19.079 --> 04:22.810
So if we wanted to find
the area of the face of one

04:22.810 --> 04:27.090
of these washers for a
given x, it's going to be--

04:27.090 --> 04:30.290
and we can factor
out this pi-- it's

04:30.290 --> 04:34.680
going to be pi times the
outer radius squared,

04:34.680 --> 04:36.540
which is all of this
business squared.

04:36.540 --> 04:41.830
So it's going to be 4 minus
x squared plus 2x squared

04:41.830 --> 04:43.280
minus pi times
the inner radius--

04:43.280 --> 04:44.780
although we factored
out the pi-- so

04:44.780 --> 04:46.810
minus the inner radius squared.

04:46.810 --> 04:51.800
So minus 4 minus x squared.

04:51.800 --> 04:57.650
So this will give us
the area of the surface

04:57.650 --> 04:59.280
or the face of one
of these washers.

04:59.280 --> 05:01.700
If we want the volume of
one of those watchers,

05:01.700 --> 05:05.040
we then just have to
multiply times the depth, dx.

05:08.010 --> 05:10.800
And then if we want to actually
find the volume of this entire

05:10.800 --> 05:14.250
figure, then we just have to
sum up all of these washers

05:14.250 --> 05:15.950
for each of our x's.

05:15.950 --> 05:16.830
So let's do that.

05:16.830 --> 05:19.050
So we're going to sum
up the washers for each

05:19.050 --> 05:21.300
of our x's and take the
limit as they approach zero,

05:21.300 --> 05:23.490
but we have to make sure
we got our interval right.

05:23.490 --> 05:26.260
So what are these-- we care
about the entire region

05:26.260 --> 05:28.840
between the points
where they intersect.

05:28.840 --> 05:30.620
So let's make sure
we get our interval.

05:30.620 --> 05:32.203
So to figure out our
interval, we just

05:32.203 --> 05:36.070
say when does y equal
x intersect y equal

05:36.070 --> 05:37.350
x squared minus 2x?

05:39.990 --> 05:41.630
Let me do this in
a different color.

05:41.630 --> 05:44.150
We just have to
think about when does

05:44.150 --> 05:46.245
x equal x squared minus 2x.

05:49.370 --> 05:51.420
When are our two functions
equal to each other?

05:51.420 --> 05:53.030
Which is equivalent
to-- if we just

05:53.030 --> 05:58.800
subtract x from
both sides, we get

05:58.800 --> 06:02.190
when does x squared
minus 3x equal 0.

06:02.190 --> 06:05.260
We can factor out an x
on the right hand side.

06:05.260 --> 06:09.530
So this is going to be when does
x times x minus 3 equal zero.

06:09.530 --> 06:12.310
Well, if the product is equal
to 0, at least one of these

06:12.310 --> 06:13.350
need to be equal to 0.

06:13.350 --> 06:18.380
So x could be equal to 0,
or x minus 3 is equal to 0.

06:18.380 --> 06:21.280
So x is equal to 0
or x is equal to 3.

06:21.280 --> 06:24.010
So this is x is 0, and
this right over here

06:24.010 --> 06:25.850
is x is equal to 3.

06:25.850 --> 06:27.100
So that gives us our interval.

06:27.100 --> 06:29.120
We're going to go
from x equals 0

06:29.120 --> 06:32.850
to x equals 3 to get our volume.

06:32.850 --> 06:35.000
In the next video,
we'll actually

06:35.000 --> 06:37.320
evaluate this integral.
